\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Comparison of weight update computation of three feed-forward spiking layers for BPTT and S-TLLR. The spiking layers are unrolled over time for both algorithms while showing the signals involved in the weight updates. The top-down learning signal for BPTT ($\frac  {\partial \mathcal  {L}}{\partial y [t]}$) is shown in green, note that at time step $t$ this learning signal depends on future time steps. In contrast, for S-TLLR the learning signal ($[\frac  {\partial \mathcal  {L}}{\partial y [t]}]_{local}$) and all the variables involved are computed with information available only the time step $t$.}}{20}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
